 "_comment": "Fixed-width artwork and spacers that live on the Thai page but are not text. The terrain-type badges Ai/La/Wa/Sp are each drawn across two 8px cells and given a full cell of advance so the halves stay on the grid they were drawn for. <MAP_L>/<MAP_R>, <B> and <P> are the weapon attribute badges, traced byte for byte from the original font at $2E8000 + code * 16 (codes $EC-$EF); they live here because leaving the raw byte to the original handler makes it claim cells out of the VWF tile pool and tear the row. <Gap> is an invisible 8px cell used to preserve value columns on status screens. <Pad> fills a fixed source span, but the parser swallows it before the renderer so it has no pixel width and allocates no dynamic tile.",
